[{:db/id 17592186151817 :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA = \\{ 2n \\mid n \\in \\mathbb{N}\\}, \\qquad\nB = \\left\\{  2^{-n} \\mid n \\in \\mathbb {N}\\right\\}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A = \\{ 2, 4, 6,\\ldots \\}$\n\nII. $A \\cap B = \\emptyset$\n\nIII. $A$ and $B$ are disjoint" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA \\cap B = \\emptyset\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\{2n∣n\\in N\\} \\\\  & =\\{2(1),2(2),2(3),…\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,4,6,…\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\{{2}^{-n}∣n\\in N\\} \\\\  & =\\{{2}^{-1},{2}^{-2},{2}^{-3},…\\} \\\\  & =\\{\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{1}{8},…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection of $A$ and $B$ is \n\n$$\nA \\cap B = \\{ 2, 4, 6, \\ldots \\} \\cap \\left\\{\\dfrac{1}{2}, \\dfrac{1}{4}, \\dfrac{1}{8},\\ldots \\right\\} = \\emptyset.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the intersection is empty, the two sets are disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152102 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5310374e-32d6-5fcc-912c-e4413b652ae5" "question-813ddd4d-da5d-5704-86ca-2482c62cc8ff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151818 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the sets are disjoint since\n\n$$\n\\{ -1, 1, \\sqrt{5} \\} \\cap \\{ v, w \\} = \\emptyset.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the disjoint union is simply the union:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{-1,1,\\sqrt{5}\\}⊔\\{v,w\\} & =\\{-1,1,\\sqrt{5}\\}\\cup \\{v,w\\} \\\\  & =\\{-1,1,\\sqrt{5},v,w\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152103 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-485ea0fb-b130-56b0-8f46-79fa4f4014b9" "question-89ecc974-5ce9-51bb-a7b1-6a66513489d0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151819 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n\\{ 7,8 \\} \\cap \\{ 2,4,8 \\} = \\{ 8 \\} \\neq \\emptyset.\n$$\n\nSo, for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{∗}=\\{(7,1),(8,1)\\} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{∗}=\\{(2,2),(4,2),(8,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2} & =\\{7,8\\}⊔\\{2,4,8\\} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{∗}\\cup {A}_{2}^{∗} \\\\  & =\\{(7,1),(8,1)\\}\\cup \\{(2,2),(4,2),(8,2)\\} \\\\  & =\\{(7,1),(8,1),(2,2),(4,2),(8,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186374289 :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA=\\{5n∣n\\in Z\\},\\,B=\\{-\\frac{1}{n}∣n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B=\\{-1,-2,-3,…\\}$\n\nII. $A\\cap B=∅$\n\nIII. $A$ and $B$ are disjoint" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is false.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\{-\\frac{1}{n}∣n\\in N\\} \\\\  & =\\{-1,-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{3},…\\} \\\\  & \\ne \\{-1,-2,-3,…\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\{5n∣n\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-10,-5,0,5,10,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\\{…,-10,-5,0,5,10,…\\}\\cap \\{-1,-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{3},…\\}=∅.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the intersection is empty, the two sets are disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186374261 :question/problem "Which of the following pairs of sets are disjoint?\n\nI. $\\{3,4,5\\}$ and $\\{6,7,8\\}$\n\nII. $\\{-4,-3,-2\\}$ and $\\{2,3,4\\}$\n\nIII. $[-3,0]$ and $[0,3]$" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Pair I is disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n\\{3,4,5\\}\\cap \\{6,7,8\\}=∅\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Pair II is also disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n\\{-4,-3,-2\\}\\cap \\{2,3,4\\}=∅\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Pair III is *not* disjoint since the intersection of the sets is not empty:\n\n$$\n[-3,0]\\cap [0,3]=\\{0\\}\\ne ∅\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5310374e-32d6-5fcc-912c-e4413b652ae5" :question/id #uuid "5310374e-32d6-5fcc-912c-e4413b652ae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-174408" :question/problem "Find the disjoint union of the sets $\\{x,y,z\\}$ and $\\{u,v,w\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the sets are disjoint since\n\n$$\n\\{x,y,z\\}\\cap \\{u,v,w\\}=∅.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the disjoint union is simply the union:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{x,y,z\\}⊔\\{u,v,w\\} & =\\{x,y,z\\}\\cup \\{u,v,w\\} \\\\  & =\\{u,v,w,x,y,z\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f552e74f-e7e5-5db8-ac8e-04cea9a16137"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f552e74f-e7e5-5db8-ac8e-04cea9a16137" :answer-field/id #uuid "f552e74f-e7e5-5db8-ac8e-04cea9a16137" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb41131f-f0ac-5da8-bab2-8c0fbf1516d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45df17b8-a416-5cc3-9ba6-f079ff754ce1" "answer-cb41131f-f0ac-5da8-bab2-8c0fbf1516d0" "answer-f39cd04a-8f84-5b13-866d-e52be5e051eb" "answer-96d8576d-cbd0-52da-a93d-bc06ecc537ed" "answer-3d09cdb8-1d37-521a-944d-5b41a7b54aca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45df17b8-a416-5cc3-9ba6-f079ff754ce1" :answer/id #uuid "45df17b8-a416-5cc3-9ba6-f079ff754ce1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,u),(y,v),(z,w)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb41131f-f0ac-5da8-bab2-8c0fbf1516d0" :answer/id #uuid "cb41131f-f0ac-5da8-bab2-8c0fbf1516d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{u,v,w,x,y,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f39cd04a-8f84-5b13-866d-e52be5e051eb" :answer/id #uuid "f39cd04a-8f84-5b13-866d-e52be5e051eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{u,v,w\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96d8576d-cbd0-52da-a93d-bc06ecc537ed" :answer/id #uuid "96d8576d-cbd0-52da-a93d-bc06ecc537ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{x,y,z\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d09cdb8-1d37-521a-944d-5b41a7b54aca" :answer/id #uuid "3d09cdb8-1d37-521a-944d-5b41a7b54aca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-813ddd4d-da5d-5704-86ca-2482c62cc8ff" :question/id #uuid "813ddd4d-da5d-5704-86ca-2482c62cc8ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-174409" :question/problem "Find the disjoint union of the sets $\\{△,◻\\}$ and $\\{a,c,e\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the sets are disjoint since\n\n$$\n\\{△,◻\\}\\cap \\{a,c,e\\}=∅.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the disjoint union is simply the union:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{△,◻\\}⊔\\{a,c,e\\} & =\\{△,◻\\}\\cup \\{a,c,e\\} \\\\  & =\\{△,◻,a,c,e\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b9f2304e-dd1d-5518-85c4-fb90e4a82856"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9f2304e-dd1d-5518-85c4-fb90e4a82856" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9f2304e-dd1d-5518-85c4-fb90e4a82856" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e906b250-7423-5dce-bd25-2c8f55f4894a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-673b6701-5f3f-56ec-a063-5d404c5e769b" "answer-17cb8dcb-70c2-5fcb-8d1a-102055731875" "answer-e906b250-7423-5dce-bd25-2c8f55f4894a" "answer-1bccda9d-f235-5f7b-808c-df1a41491109" "answer-05935852-67f3-574c-bcd8-16d04d21fd67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-673b6701-5f3f-56ec-a063-5d404c5e769b" :answer/id #uuid "673b6701-5f3f-56ec-a063-5d404c5e769b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(△,a),(△,c),(△,e),(◻,a),(◻,c),(◻,e)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17cb8dcb-70c2-5fcb-8d1a-102055731875" :answer/id #uuid "17cb8dcb-70c2-5fcb-8d1a-102055731875" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{a,c,e\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e906b250-7423-5dce-bd25-2c8f55f4894a" :answer/id #uuid "e906b250-7423-5dce-bd25-2c8f55f4894a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{△,◻,a,c,e\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bccda9d-f235-5f7b-808c-df1a41491109" :answer/id #uuid "1bccda9d-f235-5f7b-808c-df1a41491109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{△,◻\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05935852-67f3-574c-bcd8-16d04d21fd67" :answer/id #uuid "05935852-67f3-574c-bcd8-16d04d21fd67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-485ea0fb-b130-56b0-8f46-79fa4f4014b9" :question/id #uuid "485ea0fb-b130-56b0-8f46-79fa4f4014b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-174446" :question/problem "Find the disjoint union of the sets ${A}_{1}=\\{◻,△\\}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\{♡,△\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n\\{◻,△\\}\\cap \\{♡,△\\}=\\{△\\}\\ne ∅.\n$$\n\nSo, for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{∗}=\\{(◻,1),(△,1)\\} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{∗}=\\{(♡,2),(△,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2} & =\\{◻,△\\}⊔\\{♡,△\\} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{∗}\\cup {A}_{2}^{∗} \\\\  & =\\{(◻,1),(△,1)\\}\\cup \\{(♡,2),(△,2)\\} \\\\  & =\\{(◻,1),(△,1),(♡,2),(△,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-564c790a-8796-57b6-afff-883bcc976300"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-564c790a-8796-57b6-afff-883bcc976300" :answer-field/id #uuid "564c790a-8796-57b6-afff-883bcc976300" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6779eb26-6407-59f7-9e64-0e6a6276ebea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a50cc518-d784-5244-9830-60a9913eafbd" "answer-6779eb26-6407-59f7-9e64-0e6a6276ebea" "answer-fb7cf750-8daa-56f4-bb4d-0fe4dac8759a" "answer-781ef0ad-6a53-5942-aaac-760780016fe9" "answer-df2bea30-76c9-51e1-bdf3-bc6440af2ddc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a50cc518-d784-5244-9830-60a9913eafbd" :answer/id #uuid "a50cc518-d784-5244-9830-60a9913eafbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(◻,1),(△,1),(♡,1),(◻,2),(△,2),(♡,2)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6779eb26-6407-59f7-9e64-0e6a6276ebea" :answer/id #uuid "6779eb26-6407-59f7-9e64-0e6a6276ebea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(◻,1),(△,1),(♡,2),(△,2)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb7cf750-8daa-56f4-bb4d-0fe4dac8759a" :answer/id #uuid "fb7cf750-8daa-56f4-bb4d-0fe4dac8759a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(◻,♡),(◻,△),(△,♡)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-781ef0ad-6a53-5942-aaac-760780016fe9" :answer/id #uuid "781ef0ad-6a53-5942-aaac-760780016fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{◻,△,♡\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df2bea30-76c9-51e1-bdf3-bc6440af2ddc" :answer/id #uuid "df2bea30-76c9-51e1-bdf3-bc6440af2ddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{◻,♡\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-89ecc974-5ce9-51bb-a7b1-6a66513489d0" :question/id #uuid "89ecc974-5ce9-51bb-a7b1-6a66513489d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-174426" :question/problem "Find the disjoint union of the sets ${A}_{1}=\\{1,3,5\\}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\{5,10,15\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n\\{1,3,5\\}\\cap \\{5,10,15\\}=\\{5\\}\\ne ∅.\n$$\n\nSo, for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{∗}=\\{(1,1),(3,1),(5,1)\\} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{∗}=\\{(5,2),(10,2),(15,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2} & =\\{1,3,5\\}⊔\\{5,10,15\\} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{∗}\\cup {A}_{2}^{∗} \\\\  & =\\{(1,1),(3,1),(5,1)\\}\\cup \\{(5,2),(10,2),(15,2)\\} \\\\  & =\\{(1,1),(3,1),(5,1),(5,2),(10,2),(15,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4582def9-d26a-5410-99bf-96c80068a3d4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4582def9-d26a-5410-99bf-96c80068a3d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "4582def9-d26a-5410-99bf-96c80068a3d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-35d0ce44-cd7d-5d8e-a754-e982e5fe7e87" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35d0ce44-cd7d-5d8e-a754-e982e5fe7e87" "answer-2c2fddcc-c60c-559b-9b2b-f83e62067d5a" "answer-0745491e-9db4-5d8e-8d37-caa699d2ada3" "answer-1ef396c0-7d2f-5f9a-827f-d638e668dd57" "answer-c1449743-9168-5f96-9a39-81bb477b0419"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35d0ce44-cd7d-5d8e-a754-e982e5fe7e87" :answer/id #uuid "35d0ce44-cd7d-5d8e-a754-e982e5fe7e87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(1,1),(3,1),(5,1),(5,2),(10,2),(15,2)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c2fddcc-c60c-559b-9b2b-f83e62067d5a" :answer/id #uuid "2c2fddcc-c60c-559b-9b2b-f83e62067d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(1,10),(1,15),(3,10),(3,15)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0745491e-9db4-5d8e-8d37-caa699d2ada3" :answer/id #uuid "0745491e-9db4-5d8e-8d37-caa699d2ada3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(1,5),(3,10),(5,15)\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ef396c0-7d2f-5f9a-827f-d638e668dd57" :answer/id #uuid "1ef396c0-7d2f-5f9a-827f-d638e668dd57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,3,10,15\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1449743-9168-5f96-9a39-81bb477b0419" :answer/id #uuid "c1449743-9168-5f96-9a39-81bb477b0419" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,3,5,10,15\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153433 :tutorial/content "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are **disjoint** if they have no element in common. In other words, their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA \\cap B = \\emptyset\n$$\n\nFor example, consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA = \\{ -1,-2,-3 \\}, \\qquad B=\\{ 5,10 \\}\n$$\n\n \n\nThese sets are disjoint since their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B = \\{ -1,-2,-3 \\} \\cap \\{ 5,10 \\} = \\emptyset\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, $C=(-\\infty,5]$ and $D=(-2,\\infty)$ are *not* disjoint since the intersection of these sets is *not* empty:\n\n$$\nC\\cap D = (-\\infty,5] \\cap (-2,\\infty) = (-2,5] \\neq \\emptyset\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153434 :tutorial/content "The **disjoint union** of two sets is defined differently depending on whether the sets are non-overlapping (disjoint) or overlapping (have a non-empty intersection). We'll use the special symbol \"$\\sqcup$\" (square cup) to denote the disjoint union. \n\nThe disjoint union of two non-overlapping (disjoint) sets $A$ and $B$ is simply the union of the sets.\n\nFor example, since \n\n$$\n\\{ 0,2,4 \\} \\cap \\{ 1, 3 \\} = \\emptyset,\n$$\n\nwe find the disjoint union of these sets as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{0,2,4\\}⊔\\{1,3\\} & =\\{0,2,4\\}\\cup \\{1,3\\} \\\\  & =\\{0,1,2,3,4\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153436 :tutorial/content "Now, consider the following overlapping sets: \n\n$$\nA_1 = \\{ \\square, \\triangle \\}, \\qquad A_2 = \\{ \\heartsuit, \\square\\}.\n$$\n\nThese sets overlap because their intersection is non-empty. \n\n$$\nA_1 \\cap A_2 = \\{ \\square \\} \\neq \\emptyset.\n$$\n\nTo construct the disjoint union of these overlapping sets, we proceed as follows:\n\n- For each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is \"tagged\" with the corresponding index:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{∗}=\\{(◻,1),(△,1)\\} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{∗}=\\{(♡,2),(◻,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- As a result, the new sets $A_1^\\ast$ and $A_2^\\ast$ are non-overlapping. So, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2} & =\\{◻,△\\}⊔\\{♡,◻\\} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{∗}\\cup {A}_{2}^{∗} \\\\  & =\\{(◻,1),(△,1)\\}\\cup \\{(♡,2),(◻,2)\\} \\\\  & =\\{(◻,1),(△,1),(♡,2),(◻,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152373 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
